==English==
{{wikipedia|lang=en}}

===Etymology===
15th century, from {{etyl|fr|en}} {{term|fidélité|lang=fr}} from {{etyl|la|en}} {{term|fidelitas|fidēlitās|lang=la}}, from {{term|fidelis|fidēlis|faithful|lang=la}}, from {{term|fides|fidēs|faith, loyalty|lang=la}} (English {{term|faith|lang=en}}), from {{etyl|ine-pro|en}} {{recons|bʰidʰ-|lang=ine-pro}}, [[zero-grade]] of {{etyl|ine-pro|en}} {{recons|bʰeydʰ-||to command, to persuade, to trust|lang=ine-pro}} (English {{term|bide|lang=en}}).

===Noun===
{{en-noun|fidelities}}

# [[faithfulness|Faithfulness]] to one's [[duties]].
#: ''the '''fidelity''' of the civil servants''
# [[loyalty|Loyalty]] to one's [[spouse]] or [[partner]], including abstention from [[extramarital]] affairs (except in an [[open marriage]]).
# [[accuracy|Accuracy]], or exact [[correspondence]] to some given [[quality]] or [[fact]].
# The [[degree]] to which a [[system]] accurately [[reproduce]]s an input.
#* '''2003''', ''Proceedings of the Twenty-ninth International Conference on Very Large Databases, Berlin, Germany, 9-12 September, 2003'', page 58:
#*: By placing them closer to the source, we can reduce the number of messages in the system and this in turn is likely to improve the '''fidelity''' of the system.

====Quotations====
* '''2004''', ''High-'''Fidelity''' Medical Imaging Displays'' (Aldo Badano, Michael J. Flynn, Jerzy Kanicki, ISBN 0819451916)
* '''2008''', David L. Nelson, Michael M. Cox, ''Absolute Ultimate Guide for Lehninger Principles of Biochemistry'' (ISBN 1429212411), page S-305:
*: The isoleucyl-tRNA synthetase has a proofreading function that ensures the '''fidelity''' of the aminoacylation reaction, but the histidyl-tRNA synthetase lacks such a proofreading function.

